  "recipe": {
    "technique": "The technique relies on the ability of the eye and mind of the viewer to blend the color spots into a fuller range of tones. It is related to Divisionism, a more technical variant of the method. Divisionism is concerned with color theory, whereas pointillism is more focused on the specific style of brushwork used to apply the paint. Pointillism is a technique with few serious practitioners today and is notably seen in the works of Seurat, Signac, and Cross. M. Metzinger is a mosaicist like M.]."
  },
